{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Approved",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Hours of operationThe maintenance and servicing units for the Fleet&nbsp;Service Operators hereby approved shall only be active between hours of 9am to 5pm.",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be commenced before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.<br>",
    "<p>The development hereby approved shall only be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:</p><ul><li>Planning Statement (dated: 03/06/2024)</li><li>Transport Statement (received 09/10/2024)</li><li>Proposed External Details Plan (drawing re: 7825 - SMR - 09 - ZZ - DR - A - 2005 - S3 - P1, dated: 17/5/2024)</li><li>Site Location Plan (drawing ref: 7825 - SMR - 09 - ZZ - DR - A - 2001 - S3 -P1, dated: 17/05/2024)</li><li>Proposed External Details Plan (drawing ref:&nbsp;7825 - SMR - 09 - ZZ - DR - A - 2004 - S3 - P1, dated: 17/05/2024)</li><li>Proposed Site Plan (drawing ref: 7825 - SMR - 09 - ZZ - DR - A - 2003 - S3 - P2, dated: 17/05/2024)</li><li>Proposed Contextual Elevations (drawing ref:&nbsp;7825 - SMR - 09 - ZZ - DR - A - 2006 - S3 - P2, dated: 25/10/2024)</li><li>Proposed Circulation Site PLan (drawing ref:&nbsp;7825 - SMR - 09 - ZZ - DR - A - 2007 - S3 - P1, dated: 28/10/2024)</li></ul><p>No other drawings or documents apply.</p>",
    "Noise Generating Mechanical Services Plant . Before any mechanical services plant including heating, ventilation, and air\r\nconditioning (HVAC) plant to which the application refers, is used at the premises, a scheme shall be submitted to and\r\napproved in writing by the Local Planning Authority (LPA) which demonstrates that the following noise design requirements\r\ncan be complied with and shall thereafter be retained as approved.\r\na. The cumulative measured or calculated rating level of noise emitted from the mechanical services plant to which\r\nthe application refers, shall be lower than the existing background noise level by 5dB at all times when the plant is\r\nin operation.\r\nMeasurements shall be made at a height of 1.2 – 1.5 metres above the adjacent ground level and at least 3.5\r\nmetres from any sound reflecting surfaces other than the\r\nground or 1 metre from the facade of the nearest first floor (or higher) noise sensitive premises, and in\r\naccordance with the latest British Standard BS4142:2014. The\r\nmeasurement value shall be adjusted to remove the additional sound energy contribution from reflected\r\nsurfaces other than from the ground.\r\nAn alternative position for assessment /measurement may be used to allow ease of access, this must be shown\r\non a map and noise propagation calculations detailed\r\nto show how the design criteria is achieved.\r\nb. A commissioning acoustic test and report shall be undertaken within 7 days of mechanical services commissioning\r\nin order to demonstrate that condition a) above has been achieved. The results of the test shall be submitted to and\r\napproved in writing by the LPA."
  ],
